# The one fetch from outside a distribution repository, pinned.
#
# Guarden installs no artefact it has not verified, so this file is deliberately
# shipped with its digest unfilled: an unfilled pin means the fetch does not
# happen, which is the fail-closed outcome. There is no "latest" and no
# unpinned fallback, because "one third-party binary, verified" is the whole
# claim and a convenience fetch would make it false.
#
# Fill in all three from the release you mean, then `soil packages --apply`.
# The SHA256 is of the release artefact, and `soil` re-reads it on every
# `--check`, so a binary that was replaced under it is drift.
version =
url =
sha256 =
